# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 intg.cc _integrate_, approxint_exact and ck_int_numerically. A definite integral splits floor at its jumps (ceil first rewritten as -floor(-u) by ceil2floor): it finds the integers of a*x+b on the range, substitutes floor's value on each piece and adds the pieces, then checks the sum against a numeric integral (ck_int_numerically, which returns the pair [exact, numeric] when they disagree). Four faults: (1) trunc has no such rule, so once patch 0028 left trunc(u) unevaluated for an argument of unproven sign, the antiderivative x*trunc(x) was used across trunc's jumps: int(trunc(x),x,-1/2,5/2) = 3*trunc(x) (right 2), int(trunc(2*x+1),x,-3/2,1/2) = 2*trunc(2*x+1) (right 0), int(trunc(x)*x,x,-1/2,3/2) = 9/8 (right 5/8). Now, next to ceil2floor, each trunc(u) whose u contains the integration variable is rewritten (and only those: trunc(a) of an x-free a stays) as floor(u)+(1-sign(u))/2 (evaluated), which is trunc(u) off the integers of u, so the integral is the same; the split cuts at every integer of u, 0 included, and sign(u) is constant on each piece; trunc(x,n) is left as it was. (2) For a falling a*x+b (a < 0, so every ceil, and trunc of a proven negative, which is -floor(-u)) from a non-integer start u0 the first jump was taken where a*x+b reaches floor(u0)-1, one interval late: int(ceil(x),x,1/2,3/2) = [1,1.5] (right 3/2), int(floor(-x),x,-3/2,-1/2) = [1,0.5] (right 1/2), int(trunc(x),x,-5/2,0) = [-4,-1.99999850795] (right -2). Now the first jump is where a*x+b reaches floor(u0); from an integer start it is as before. (3) The numeric check took trunc as exactly integrable (approxint_exact: sign, floor, ceil and round are not) and evaluated x*trunc(x) at the ends (5.0 for the first integral). Now trunc goes to the adaptive quadrature as floor does. (4) tegral stops at an error of 1e-6 relative to the integral of |f|, but an exact value 0 had to meet a numeric value below 1e-8: int(trunc(x),x,-3/2,3/2) = [0,-2.885e-07]. Now an exact value below 1e-8 is kept when the numeric value is at most 1e-5 times the integral of |f| (computed only then). limit(trunc(x),x,-1,1) = -1 (right 0) is another path (series.cc; trunc has no series rule and is not in sign_floor_ceil_round_tab) and is not changed.
